  note = {verified 2026-09-10 (paper lap 29): the concept DOI above was opened and redirects to the Zenodo record, whose landing page and full abstract were read. ⚠ NOT YET CITED BY THE MANUSCRIPT, and the reason is the length proxy, not the source. This is the closest architecture-level comparator the project has found (WFG-239, filed by the research lap of 2026-09-10; docs/auto/research/IEEE_PLAN.md G11) and §2 owes it a line, but the cheapest honest form of that line measures +26 body words with the builder's own counter against a margin of 2 (NH-037, open). The entry is added now because CHARTER §12 requires whoever cites a work to have opened it, and this lap could; a later lap should not have to re-open it to spend the words. What the record states: resource type "Preprint", deposit date 9 September 2026, five creators with Kale, Dilip marked "(Supervisor)". ⚠ The page's own DOI field reads 10.5281/zenodo.22668358 — that is the VERSION DOI of the same record and not a duplicate deposit, which critic #61 re-derived independently for this record and for the Choi & Chae deposit (22069027 returns ...22069028); the CONCEPT DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22668357 is the one cited here. The abstract states verbatim: "modern predictive frameworks utilizing end-to-end deep learning often succumb to persistence bias, wherein models achieve high statistical accuracy by propagating current fire states forward while ignoring fluid dynamics"; "We engineered a multimodal dataset targeting the topographical variations of Uttarakhand, India, and use it to show empirically that neither a recurrent nor a non-recurrent network learns to advect fire past the persistence baseline"; "a lightweight U-Net supplies a per-cell flammability prior, and an explicit Cellular Automaton physics engine executing within PyTorch performs the temporal spread that the networks could not learn"; "The system orchestrates OpenRouteService vector routing using spatial polygon clustering"; and "the system delegates to an internal D* Lite heuristic grid fallback that incrementally routes traffic away from actively predicted fires". ⚠ BOUNDARIES, which belong in any sentence that cites this and not in a footnote: Uttarakhand, India; a road and vehicle routing stack; an unrefereed preprint; and NO reported evaluation metric of any kind, for the spread model or the routing layer — the record states none and none was read, so no accuracy comparison may be made in either direction and no number from it is registered anywhere in this repository. ⚠ Its abstract closes on "guaranteed safe evacuation"; nothing in this manuscript may imitate that claim, this project existing partly to measure why no such guarantee is available. The 2.5 MB attached PDF was not retrieved (the research lap of 2026-09-10 records the same), so nothing here rests on its contents}
}

